D = {
 "Silvanus|FRHOF": "Silvanus is the Oak Father, god of wild nature in all its forms, from forests to deserts. He values balance and holds that untamed nature is the true state of the world. His mostly druid followers resist settlements pushing into the wild and see wasteful use of resources as blasphemy. Shrines are oak groves or an oak leaf carved into bark, and temples are rare and hidden deep in forests.",
 "Sirrion|DSOTDQ": "Sirrion is a passionate, impulsive god of alchemy, transformation, lucky invention, and flame. He stands for sudden excitement that flares fast and smolders long. His followers treat strong emotion as a way to express the divine.",
 "Solinari|DSOTDQ": "Solinari is the god of good magic and patron of the White Robes and other kindly mages. His power shines through the white moon of Krynn, the brightest of three. With his cousins Lunitari and Nuitari, he encourages magic that helps, heals, and protects.",
 "Sseth|VGM": "Sseth, the Sibilant Death, is a winged yuan-ti god who promised to restore the fading yuan-ti empire in return for worship. Many followers of Merrshaulk shifted to him. His devoted mind whisperers copy his methods by offering alternatives to rival plans, and they act self-important enough that other yuan-ti find them distasteful.",
 "Sune|FRHOF": "Sune Firehair is the god of beauty, passion, and the pleasures of the senses. Her followers hold that enjoying beauty is an act of worship, and that true beauty comes from within. They believe in romance and following the heart. Her temples serve as public baths and salons, and the knightly Sodality of the Ruby Rose guards her holy places.",
 "Takhisis|DSOTDQ": "Takhisis is the Dragon Queen, leader of Krynn's evil gods and ruler of chromatic dragons. She is the god of power, pride, and control, and she tempts mortals with promises of dominance over others. She may appear as a dark-haired armored warrior, but her true form is a five-headed dragon.",
 "Talona|FRHOF": "Talona, the Mistress of Disease, is a petulant god of plague and poison who demands placation. Mortals pray to her only during epidemics, so she has few temples and lashes out again when ignored. Her priests often join unwillingly, such as plague survivors. Her sign is three droplets in a triangle, and fanatics brew poison and spread contagion in her name.",
 "Talos|FRHOF": "Talos, the Storm Lord, is the god of storms, fire, earthquakes, and wanton destruction. Raiders and brigands follow him and teach that life is chaos, so one should seize what one can. His worship is outlawed in most places. Priests wander like storms in ragged robes with gold and silver stitching, and many wear an eye patch.",
 "Tempus|FRHOF": "Tempus, the Foehammer, is a war god who favors all sides at random. He backs bravery, settling disputes by force, and swift, decisive battles. His priests spread Tempus's Honor, a code that includes arming those in need, honoring foes, and sparing noncombatants. Soldiers and battlefield chaplains revere him, and the mercenary Stormknives follow a four-part loyalty code.",
 "Tharizdun|EGW": "Tharizdun is the Chained Oblivion, a mad god of endless darkness and destruction, imprisoned deep in the Abyss. Its dreams spawn demons and aberrations. Its cultists work without word from it and await the Epoch of Ends. They offer power to it, restore forgotten shrines, and ruin the world. Followers of Ioun work to keep it bound.",
 "Thassa|MOT": "Thassa is the Theros god of the sea, its creatures, and the unknown depths. She governs slow, irresistible change and opposes any attempt to fix a permanent order. Patient but terrible when angered, she is worshiped mostly by tritons, sailors, and coastal folk, who pray at high and low tide. Her favored animal is the crab.",
 "The Devourer|ERLW": "The Devourer is the Sovereign Host's dark power of destructive nature, both raw elemental force and bestial savagery.",
 "The Fury|ERLW": "The Fury governs passion and revenge, rage and despair. She offers vengeance to the wronged, though it usually brings more suffering.",
 "The Hag Mother|EGW": "The Hag Mother is said to be the oldest hag and the source of all others, cursed and bound to Exandria by her first coven. She wanders in disguise and offers power to people in dire need in exchange for service. Her tasks are dangerous and sometimes cruel, and some create new hags. Her true goal is known only to her.",
 "The Keeper|ERLW": "The Keeper is a dark power who snatches souls before they reach Dolurrh and hoards them along with great wealth. The greedy take him as patron, and his priests often work as criminal fixers.",
 "The Luxon|EGW": "The Luxon is the central deity of the Kryn Dynasty, a being of light with no active mind or personality. Worship is faith backed by study of the beacons and dunamis, and its priests study dunamantic magic. Followers carry small dodecahedrons as symbols. Kryn teaching says the Luxon sacrificed its essence to make beacons that cycle souls through rebirth to learn what the Luxon is.",
 "The Mockery|ERLW": "The Mockery is the patron of treachery and battlefield terror, guiding warriors and assassins who win by guile. He was once a brother of Dol Dorn and Dol Arrah, but was stripped of his skin and name after betraying them.",
 "The Raven Queen|EGW": "The Raven Queen is the god of death and fate, and the only known mortal to become a god. She guards the border between life and death and protects the dead from undeath. Her holy day is the Night of Ascension. Her tenets say death is natural, fate is sacred, and undeath is an atrocity to be torn down.",
 "The Red Knight|FRHOF": "The Red Knight, the Lady of Strategy, is the war god of planning and tactics rather than bravery or pain. Calm and logical but compassionate, she is a counselor to Tempus. Commanders, war college instructors, quartermasters, and tactics authors revere her. Her priests, the Red Fellowship, teach strategy to leaders, and her temples hold enchanted war tables.",
 "The Shadow|ERLW": "The Shadow is the dark side of knowledge and ambition, said to be Aureon's shadow, born when Aureon mastered magic. It makes monsters, keeps forbidden secrets, and gives malevolent spells to warlocks and wizards.",
 "The Traveler|EGW": "The Traveler is Artagan, a selfish and anarchic archfey exiled by Corellon after a prank and now posing as a god. Eccentric and impulsive, he wanders Exandria seeking entertaining followers and grants fey magic as divine boons. It is unclear whether he wants real godhood or is just playing a game.",
 "The Traveler|ERLW": "The Traveler is a trickster who teaches that chaos drives evolution and change makes us stronger. Some artificers worship him as lord of innovation, but his gifts always carry unexpected consequences.",
 "Tiamat|EGW": "Tiamat is the evil queen of dragons and god of greed, envy, and hoarded wealth. Chromatic dragons fear her, and any who crave wealth may worship her. She is imprisoned in Avernus and seeks to break free. Her creed says to hoard gold, avenge every slight, and take what you covet. Bahamut's paladins hunt her cults.",
 "Torm|FRHOF": "Torm is the god of courage, duty, and self-sacrifice, and a patron of many paladins. Kind to the weak and stern to evil, he teaches that brave service pleases him and every failure of duty dims him. His followers keep order and oppose corruption. He forms the Triad with Tyr and Ilmater, and the Order of the Golden Lion atones for old persecutions.",
 "Torog|EGW": "Torog, the Crawling King, is the dark god of tunnels and caverns beneath Exandria, patron of torturers, slavers, and jailers. Pelor and Raei defeated and imprisoned him beyond the world. His creed says to exalt lightless places, relish pain given and received, and drag all life into the dark.",
 "Tymora|SCAG": "Tymora, Lady Luck, is the goddess of fortune, loved by gamblers and risk takers. Her motto is that fortune favors the bold. Her faith needs few priests or temples, though gambling parlors often host shrines. Folk avoid praying to her and Beshaba together. She and Beshaba were born when Tyche split in two.",
 "Tyr|FRHOF": "Tyr, the Evenhanded, is the god of justice, a blindfolded warrior who lost his right hand to Kezef. His followers seek truth, right wrongs, and punish the guilty by a strict code of law and honesty, while not judging failures too harshly. Knights, judges, and priests wear thin cloth over their eyes, and he seldom speaks directly to mortals.",
 "Uk'otoa|EGW": "Uk'otoa is a giant sea serpent made by Zehir and later worshiped as a god by the Ki'Nau of the Swavain Islands. Zehir had him sealed beneath the Lucidian Ocean. He now sends dreams to sailors, offering arcane gifts and the Sword of Fathoms to those who will free him, in loose accord with Desirat and Quajath.",
 "Umberlee|FRHOF": "Umberlee, the Wavemother, is the cruel and capricious sea god, worshiped out of fear. Sailors toss gems overboard to calm storms, and coastal towns hold festivals to appease her. Her disorganized priests warn of doom and demand free passage, and use the preserved hand of a drowned person as a holy symbol. Some druids honor her as nature at its cruelest.",
 "Urdlen|MTF": "Urdlen, the Glutton, is the gnome god of greed, envy, and selfishness, exiled by Garl for refusing to join an important quest. He later became a blind, hairless mole monster with iron claws. Gnomes see his influence in jealousy and petulance, and his tales warn of the cost of staying apart from others.",
 "Urogalan|MTF": "Urogalan is the halfling god of the dead. He went into the afterlife and returned, then described the Green Fields where ancestors rest and watch over family. Halflings look for signs from lost loved ones. He guides the dead with his black hound and a magic lantern, and his gaunt, melancholy priests wear white robes.",
 "Vecna|EGW": "Vecna is the Whispered One, the dark god of necromancy, undeath, and secrets, a former lich archmage who became a god and was sealed behind the Divine Gate. He hates all gods, especially Ioun. His creed says to hoard knowledge, reveal only part of it, cultivate evil, and ruin worshipers of other gods.",
 "Vesh|EGW": "Vesh is an ancient being, witch or demigod, who seduces those who seek forbidden magic. Her cults hold hedonistic rites that end in her choosing a mate. She slaughters the rest, lends strength to the chosen, and demands their full devotion. Her moods swing between cruelty and mercy, so seekers of her favor commit terrible acts.",
 "Vhaeraun|MTF": "Vhaeraun is the drow god of arrogance, theft, and self-advancement, Lolth's favored son. His followers take what they want by stealth or force and always wear masks in public. Some quietly see him as an advocate of equality for male and female drow, a heresy Lolth's priestesses crush.",
 "Waukeen|FRHOF": "Waukeen, the Coinmaiden, is the god of wealth and trade who supports anything that boosts commerce. Merchants, caravan guides, peddlers, and smugglers worship her. She frowns on misers and monopolies, and her only real enemy is Mask. Followers often set aside ten percent of profits to back struggling businesses or new ventures.",
 "Xalicas|EGW": "Xalicas is a solar, once the right hand of the Arch Heart, blinded and unable to fly after the Calamity. She now wanders Wildemount atoning and trying to prevent another great war. Her followers heal war-scarred lands and repair nature, and she lends power to those who stop needless war, resist tyranny, and defend the innocent.",
 "Yondalla|MTF": "Yondalla is the halfling goddess who adopted the timid early halflings, gathered them, and taught them to build, plant, and harvest. She hid their villages from plunderers and raised the best halflings to godhood as the rest of the pantheon. Halflings credit her for good luck, bountiful gardens, and bad luck turned good.",
 "Yurtrus|VGM": "Yurtrus is the silent orc god of death and disease, a rotting figure with pure white hands. His followers live at the edge of the tribe and handle the dead, adding bones to ossuary shrines. His White Hand shamans wield taboo death magic. His priests send fallen heroes to Gruumsh by preparing their skulls, and diseased nurtured ones spread plague among enemies.",
 "Zeboim|DSOTDQ": "Zeboim is the god of the ocean's destructive side, including storms and dangerous sea creatures. She is mercurial, and even her followers suffer her rage. Most sailors pray to Habbakuk to hold her back, but some give her offerings to ease her anger.",
 "Zehir|EGW": "Zehir is the evil god of poisons, assassins, and darkness, creator of snakes and serpentkin. Serpentkin worship him, and his surviving followers use poison and fire to undermine civilization and nature. He hates Erathis and Melora. His creed says to act in secret, strike without reason, and kill slowly and painfully.",
 "Zinzerena|MTF": "Zinzerena is the drow patron of assassination, illusion, and lies, a stealthy trickster who waits for foes to weaken. Her faith survives in folk tales among commoners, servants, and outcast nobles with a rebellious streak. She approves of arcane study, so female drow who pursue magic in secret find tutors in her cult.",
 "Zivilyn|DSOTDQ": "Zivilyn embodies the calm wisdom needed to use knowledge well, existing in all times and places and holding the wisdom of every plane. Eccentrics, philosophers, and sages often worship him.",
}
